<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chengpu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">632 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chengpu was fought in 632 BCE in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> between the State of Jin, under Duke Wen, with its allies Qi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>, and the forces of Chu and its allies. Jin's victory, won by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feigned-retreat">feigned retreat</a> and attacks on the weaker Chu wings, halted Chu's advance into the north and made Duke Wen hegemon of the Zhou states. The battle is described in detail in the Zuo zhuan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-chengpu.jpg" alt="Battle of Chengpu" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Chengpu.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
